se,"url":"https://scambs.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Commercial property portfolio delivering \u00a3377k less revenue than planned, driven by vacancies and project delays","lead":"The council's commercial property portfolio is materially underperforming, affecting the reliability of commercial revenue as a funding source for its budget.","iso":"2026-09-29","paper_title":"Appendix A - Efficiency Proposals Update 2026-27","paper_url":"https://scambs.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s144463/144463.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Government policy announcements (LGR and GCDC) blocking \u00a3125k of planned commercial income","lead":"Government policy announcements are creating material barriers to the council's revenue plans, demonstrating that external policy uncertainty directly threatens the council's financial resilience.","iso":"2026-09-29","paper_title":"Appendix A - Efficiency Proposals Update 2026-27","paper_url":"https://scambs.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s144463/144463.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"The 42% net service cost underspend is substantially explained by \u00a31.4 million carried-forward grants and timing differences, not real budget overperformance.","lead":"A lender must distinguish real budget performance from timing noise; the council's transparency prevents misinterpretation of financial position.","iso":"2026-09-29","paper_title":"Q1 - Fin Rpt","paper_url":"https://scambs.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s144462/144462.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix A - Efficiency Proposals Update 2026-27","paper_url":"https://scambs.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s144463/144463.pdf","headline":"Commercial property portfolio delivering \u00a3377k less revenue than planned, driven by vacancies and project delays","detail":"Economic Development commercial property revenue is forecasting \u00a355k against a \u00a3400k proposal (\u00a3345k shortfall, rated AMBER) due to vacant units and prospective occupier engagement delays; full recovery is deferred to 2027-28. South Cambs Connect ground floor lettings are also behind plan at \u00a318k against a \u00a350k proposal (\u00a332k shortfall, rated AMBER) due to ongoing work on the charging plan. Combined, the commercial property portfolio is \u00a3377k short of plan.","category":"income","matters":"The council's commercial property portfolio is materially underperforming, affecting the reliability of commercial revenue as a funding source for its budget.","figures":"Economic Development: \u00a3400k proposal, \u00a355k forecast (\u00a3345k shortfall); South Cambs Connect: \u00a350k proposal, \u00a318k forecast (\u00a332k shortfall)","quote":"One unit remains vacant, and a further unit has recently become vacant. Work is ongoing with prospective occupiers to secure occupancy of the empty units. It is therefore anticipated that the full income will not be realised in 2026/27, with a proportion now expected to be received in 2027/28.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix A - Efficiency Proposals Update 2026-27","paper_url":"https://scambs.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s144463/144463.pdf","headline":"Government policy announcements (LGR and GCDC) blocking \u00a3125k of planned commercial income","detail":"The Local Government Reorganisation announcement has made prospective tenants unwilling to enter multi-year lease agreements, eliminating the expected \u00a3100k of rental income at South Cambs Hall (proposal to \u00a30 forecast, rated RED). Similarly, the Greater Cambridge Development Corporation announcement has halted preparatory work for \u00a325k of Built and Natural Environment Service additional income (proposal to \u00a30, rated RED). Combined, these government announcements are preventing \u00a3125k of planned revenue from being realised.","category":"income","matters":"Government policy announcements are creating material barriers to the council's revenue plans, demonstrating that external policy uncertainty directly threatens the council's financial resilience.","figures":"South Cambs Hall: \u00a3100k proposal to \u00a30 forecast; BNE: \u00a325k proposal to \u00a30 forecast","quote":"Due to the announcement of Local Government Reorganisation (LGR), no new tenants are currently expected to occupy the vacant space, as prospective occupiers are generally unwilling to enter into lease agreements with terms of less than two years.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Q1 - Fin Rpt","paper_url":"https://scambs.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s144462/144462.pdf","headline":"The 42% net service cost underspend is substantially explained by \u00a31.4 million carried-forward grants and timing differences, not real budget overperformance.","detail":"While net service costs show \u00a32.094m underspend (42%), the council carried \u00a31.4m of grant income from 2025/26 into the current year. The council explicitly warns that Q1 position is not a reliable guide to final outturn, with variances largely reflecting phased service delivery and timing of income and expenditure.","category":"other","matters":"A lender must distinguish real budget performance from timing noise; the council's transparency prevents misinterpretation of financial position.","figures":"\u00a32,094,000 underspend (42% of net service costs); \u00a31.4 million grant carry-forward from 2025/26","quote":"The Council has carried forward \u00a31.4 million of grant income from 2025/26, resulting in income levels above the approved budget... The position at the end of June 202 6 is not necessarily a good guide to the final outturn and needs to be treated as such.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Q1 - Fin Rpt","paper_url":"https://scambs.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s144462/144462.pdf","headline":"Efficiency proposals totalling \u00a3734,000 are on track with no areas of concern identified.","detail":"The council included \u00a3734,000 of efficiency proposals in the 2026/27 budget comprising ongoing savings and income generation. Q1 monitoring confirms no further areas of concern, indicating the planned budget reductions are being delivered.","category":"savings","matters":"A lender must verify the council's planned savings are materializing; their delivery is essential to financial sustainability.","figures":"\u00a3734,000 efficiency proposals","quote":"The original budget for 202 6/27 included efficiency proposals totalling \u00a3 734,000 comprising of ongoing savings and income generation... there are no further areas of concern at this stage.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix B - Corporate Outturn 2026-27","paper_url":"https://scambs.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s144464/144464.pdf","headline":"General Fund investment income outperforming budget by \u00a396k (+4% favorable variance)","detail":"Treasury management generated \u00a32,313k actual investment income against \u00a32,217k budget, a \u00a396k outperformance in Q1. This reflects better-than-budgeted returns on cash balances, likely due to higher prevailing interest rates.","category":"income","matters":"A lender would see better treasury returns as improving the council's cash reserves and financial resilience, though this benefit is likely temporary and dependent on interest rates remaining elevated.","figures":"Budgeted \u00a32,217k; actual \u00a32,313k; outperformance \u00a396k","quote":"Investment Income (8,770) (2,217) (2,313) (96) -4%","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-17"},"name":"South Cambridgeshire","findings_total":83,"news_drafts_total":3}}